## Usage

```bash
npm install
npm test       # run tests
npm run build  # emit dist/
```

```ts
import { capitalize, truncate } from "string-utils";

capitalize("world");           // "World"
truncate("A long sentence", 9); // "A long..."
```

**Design notes:** Each function lives in its own file so tests map 1:1 to source, and `index.ts` acts as the single public entry point. Tests live in a separate `tests/` folder so they're excluded from the `tsc` build (via `rootDir: "src"`). If you prefer colocated tests (`src/capitalize.test.ts`), just update the vitest `include` and add `"exclude": ["**/*.test.ts"]` to `tsconfig.json`.

