Note: the custom suffix test above is needlessly convoluted. Simpler and clearer:

```ts
it("supports a custom suffix", () => {
  expect(truncate("hello world", 7, "…")).toBe("hello …");
});
```
Here `"hello "` is 6 characters plus `…` equals 7, so the expected value is `"hello …"`. Use this version.

