## Key conventions

**Command module contract** — every file in `src/commands/` exports the same three things, so `cli.js` can treat them uniformly:

```js
// src/commands/add.js
export const name = 'add';
export const description = 'Add one or more items to a tally';
export const options = {
  count: { type: 'int', default: 1, short: 'c' },
};

export async function action(items, flags, ctx) {
  const tally = await ctx.store.load();
  for (const item of items) tally.add(item, flags.count);
  await ctx.store.save(tally);
  ctx.log(`Added ${items.length} item(s).`);
}
```

**Registry** — `src/commands/index.js` is the only place that knows the full command list:

```js
import * as add from './add.js';
import * as list from './list.js';
import * as remove from './remove.js';
import * as clear from './clear.js';
import * as stats from './stats.js';

export const commands = [add, list, remove, clear, stats];
export const byName = new Map(commands.map((c) => [c.name, c]));
