## Conventions worth enforcing

| Concern | Rule |
|---|---|
| Command file | Exports a factory `makeXCommand({ store, logger })` **and** a default-wired instance. |
| Business logic | Lives in `src/core/` and is pure — no `fs`, no `process`, no `console`. |
| Side effects | Only `src/io/` touches the filesystem; `src/util/logger.js` only writes to stderr. |
| Output | Human-readable text → stdout; diagnostics/warnings → stderr. Keeps piping sane. |
| Errors | Throw `CliError` with an `exitCode`; `bin/tally.js` is the only place that maps errors to exit codes. |
| Tests | Mirror `src/` paths under `test/unit/`; integration tests live in `test/integration/` and spawn the real binary. |
| Adding a command | New file in `src/commands/` + one import line in `src/commands/index.js` + one test file. No other file changes. |

## Variations

- **TypeScript**: rename `src/` → `src/`, add `tsconfig.json`, compile to `dist/`, point `bin`/`exports` at `dist/`, and keep `test/**/*.test.ts` alongside. The structure above is unchanged.
- **Vitest/Jest**: replace `node:test` imports with `describe/it/expect`; add `vitest.config.js` with `test.include: ['test/**/*.test.js']` and `coverage.include: ['src/**']`.
- **Plugins/subcommands from other packages**: `src/commands/index.js` can merge in an array contributed via `src/plugins.js`, keeping the registry the single extension point.

